          "title": "You'll want to know: recitare",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "recitare — \"to act; to recite\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Recito in una compagnia di teatro amatoriale. I act in an amateur theatre company."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "More than to recite: on stage it means to act."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "recitare is a learned borrowing from Latin recitāre \"to read aloud\" (EtymDB), from citāre \"to call\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
